Description:

The HTTP server supports Content-Digest and Want-Content-Digest (RFC 9530),
with the sha-256 and sha-512 algorithms.  A response carries Content-Digest
when the request's Want-Content-Digest asks for it, as a trailer for a
chunked response, and a request whose Content-Digest doesn't match its
content is refused with 400.  A Want-Content-Digest supersedes
httpcontentmd5: the response carries the Content-Digest asked for instead of
Content-MD5.

The HTTP server also supports Unencoded-Digest and Want-Unencoded-Digest
(draft-ietf-httpbis-unencoded-digest), whose digest is of the
representation without any content coding, such as compression.


